  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{x}{ln\u2061x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u=x$ and $v=ln\u2061x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(ln\u2061x\\cdot 1-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x})}{{(ln\u2061x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{ln\u2061x-1}{{(ln\u2061x)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
